# gen-doc-index.dl — dogfoods the doc tools on v5's own docs + source.
#
# Three tools exercised together in one program:
#   doc_node — the markdown-structure relation (headings, via ingest::IngestLang)
#   comment  — rule-driven region extractor over Rust //! module docs
#   gen      — splice the derived index back between the markers below
#
# This is the query-time unification of doc space and code space: doc_node
# reads markdown structure, comment reads source comment regions, and both feed
# one gen splice. No doc_ref edge relation needed; the two ops share a rule.
#
# Run from the repo root:  dl examples/gen-doc-index.dl
# Rerun converges (no write when the bytes already match). The block below is live.
#
